From b2de4de4aa7901f6f4dc9c0b91f1e6fd3c375cd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: P2ppyJack <P2ppyJack@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 17:46:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat(journey): cross-profile memory consolidation +
 reconcile with api/* modules

Fold the desktop/bot recall + insert fixes onto the refactored desktop API
layer (hermes.ts monolith -> api/* modules). Re-homes the journey gateway
helpers into api/skills.ts so they ride the new barrel re-exports.

Features
- Multi-profile star map: a bot selector merges several profiles' graphs into
  one view; nodes/edges/cards carry a source `profile` tag and profile-prefixed
  ids so a fact's origin is always visible.
- Cross-profile insert: copy a memory node (incl. Honcho conclusions) from one
  bot into another bot's MEMORY.md, with an [Imported from profile: X]
  provenance note. Skills are intentionally not cross-insertable.
- Recall drafts now scope to the node's OWN profile (fixes prefixed-id 404 when
  recalling from a merged multi-profile graph).

Fixes
- cross-insert wrote <home>/MEMORY.md but the graph reads
  <home>/memories/MEMORY.md -> insert silently never showed. Now writes the
  graph-visible file (regression test added).

Tests: tsc clean; vitest 61/61 (starmap+i18n); pytest 23/23 (learning +
cross-insert). Windows-footgun scan clean (11 files).
